---
// HOME DARK REFRAME — full-width photographic authority band. Built for the 2026-09-03 homepage
// composition rebuild (docs/05-DECISIONS-LOG.md, "Homepage section count reopened"), which asks
// for a full-width dark reframe section as a meaningful visual break, matching the reference
// sites' (911 Bio Clean, ClearPath) alternating light/dark rhythm.
//
// Uses PhotoAuthorityBand (built same day) for the full-cover-image + solid-navy-overlay
// treatment. COPY IS THE APPROVED LEDE FROM docs/aseptaclean-all-website-copy.md's "Show us the
// condition first." passage — the same sentence OperatingEvidence.astro already used as its
// section lede. Only the first paragraph (heading + lede) moves here; the Property Handoff
// Record artifact and its supporting paragraphs stay in OperatingEvidence-derived content
// elsewhere on the page (see HomeServiceArea/founder sections) rather than being duplicated.
import PhotoAuthorityBand from "@components/PhotoAuthorityBand.astro";
import reframeImage from "../assets/homepage/service-development-cleanup-asurnipal.jpg";
---

<PhotoAuthorityBand
  image={reframeImage}
  imageAlt="Reference photograph of a dining room where accumulated household contents cover the table, sideboard and floor."
  headingId="dark-reframe-title"
>
  <h2 id="dark-reframe-title" class="ac-type-h2">Show us the condition first.</h2>
  <p>
    Difficult property cleanup rarely fits a standard checklist. Two homes can look similar and
    need completely different work. We look at what is actually there before deciding what the
    work should involve.
  </p>
  <p class="home-dark-reframe__note">
    Development reference photograph &middot; not Aseptaclean project work &middot; Asurnipal,
    Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0
  </p>
</PhotoAuthorityBand>

<style>
  .home-dark-reframe__note {
    margin-top: 20px;
    color: rgb(255 255 255 / 52%);
    font-size: 0.6875rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    letter-spacing: 0.055em;
    line-height: 1.5;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
</style>
